rker's partition. This supports the worker in identifying and processing the appropriate database entries for each micro-cycle. If all required processing is completed within a partition, the worker logs successful partition completion.\n\n\nThe worker's operational logic divides into a main loop managing cycles of element idea generation, prompt escalation, and SEO tasks. It prioritizes tasks based on database queries for elements needing ideas, escalated prompts, or SEO metadata. Each micro-cycle processes a random number of items within assigned partitions.\n\nEach micro-cycle includes checks to verify the active time limit. The worker saves its progress periodically. The sleep cycle is a longer period of operation, followed by rest, which provides some degree of resource management and ensures the worker doesn't operate indefinitely.\n\n\nA delay ladder is implemented within each micro-cycle, increasing the delay between tasks to avoid overloading resources. Failure conditions trigger a longer pause before retrying.\n\nUpon completing a micro-cycle batch target, the worker enters a rest period of random duration, logging its status and progress to persistent storage. This cycle is repeated.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/Youtube Automation/PromptDatabase/run_cluster_pipeline.py","ContentOffset":0,"EndLine":85,"StartLine":60,"toolAction":"Viewing execute_db_write in run_cluster_pipeline.py","toolSummary":"View execute_db_write"}}]}
